# Deny-all allowlist: ONLY the paths explicitly re-included below can enter the
# build context. Everything else is unreachable no matter what a developer has
# lying around in their working tree — notably the host `.venv` (~150MB of
# macOS/arm64 binaries that would corrupt the Linux venv built in stage 1),
# plus `.git`, `.env`, `*.pem` private keys, `gcp/` Terraform, `tests/`, `.github/`
# and the docs. This is why `COPY . .` is safe here.
**

# Application code and dependency manifests — the only things the image needs.
!app/**
!run.py
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version

# Bytecode scrubbing, deliberately listed AFTER the allowlist so it takes
# precedence (in .dockerignore the last matching rule wins): without these,
# `!app/**` would re-admit stale host `__pycache__`/*.pyc from the tree.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
